  "hypothesis_statement": "A causally executable, side-aware Bollinger middle-band mean-reversion exit applied after unchanged baseline entries reduces MFE-to-exit leakage and improves net economics versus the immutable stop-dominated baseline exit path, without changing entry eligibility, direction/side selection, instrument selection, sizing, risk, execution, or canonical 1.0x costs.",
  "scientific_hypothesis": "On the sealed DEVELOPMENT_ONLY Bollinger/MR baseline, material EXIT_LEAKAGE arises because open positions often hold past mean-reversion and exit via stop_loss after giving back favorable excursion. Enforcing a deterministic side-aware middle-band exit at finalized PT1H bars, using only already-bound Bollinger parameters (bb_period=20, bb_std=2.0, exit_level=middle), improves MFE capture and net PF/net pnl versus the identical control chain.",
  "economic_hypothesis": "Relative to the immutable bollinger_bands/v2 canonical baseline on the sealed DEVELOPMENT_ONLY panel at frozen 1.0x costs, the treatment yields jointly: net_profit_factor_treatment > control, net_pnl_treatment > control (equivalently net_return_treatment > control), and mean_realized_pnl_over_mfe_capture_ratio_treatment > control, without improvement explained solely by reduced trade_count or artificially lower turnover, without new instrument concentration, and without any cost assumption below canonical 1.0x.",
  "primary_decision_metric": "NET_PROFIT_FACTOR",
  "primary_decision_metric_contract": "PASS requires joint satisfaction of all pass_requires_all checks; NET_PROFIT_FACTOR is the lead economic decision metric (treatment > control), with net_pnl/net_return, MFE capture, leakage, turnover/trade-count guardrails, side/instrument attribution, and canonical cost freeze as hard companions.",
